WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:02.760
- Troy and I met our
sophomore year in high school,

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:05.240
but it wasn't until the
beginning of our senior year

00:00:05.240 --> 00:00:09.013
that I was like hey, I
think he should ask me out.

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:12.253
I'm done being friends, yeah.

00:00:13.670 --> 00:00:17.960
On January 1st, 2001,
Troy got down on his knee

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:20.750
and said I was his best friend, and that

00:00:20.750 --> 00:00:23.010
he wanted to spend his life with me.

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:24.593
How could I say no to that?

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:30.173
In 2016, I was diagnosed
with breast cancer.

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:37.103
Talk about not knowing what to do.

00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:41.870
Troy has been by my side
through every step of the way.

00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:46.073
He has cried with me,
took care of our two boys.

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:50.880
He has held me up.

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:55.880
Then in April of 2017, I
was declared cancer free.

00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:00.480
Our hearts were just so full,
and everybody was so happy.

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:04.863
And we decided to go to Route
91 Country Festival in Vegas.

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:07.840
(screaming)

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:10.495
At first I heard what I
thought were fireworks.

00:01:10.495 --> 00:01:12.850
(ambulance siren)

00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:15.783
Troy knew at that time that
somebody was shooting at us.

00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:18.390
Troy reached over to get me out,

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:21.090
and we were holding hands
when he got shot in the leg.

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:24.950
Troy not only saved my life that night,

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:28.810
but he was credited for
saving another 20 people.

00:01:28.810 --> 00:01:31.130
He was awarded his second Medal of Valor

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:33.050
for what he did that night.

00:01:33.050 --> 00:01:35.710
Troy is an amazing man, and I love him

00:01:35.710 --> 00:01:37.747
more than any words could ever say.

00:01:38.688 --> 00:01:42.170
(audience cheering)

00:01:42.170 --> 00:01:44.290
- Well Shannon is joining us now, y'all.

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:45.745
Give it up for Shannon!

00:01:45.745 --> 00:01:48.197
(audience cheering)

00:01:48.197 --> 00:01:51.600
So in my time spent with you,

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:52.750
this is one of my favorite stories.

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:54.700
Troy was almost the man that got away.

00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:56.440
Do you wanna tell everyone how?

00:01:56.440 --> 00:02:00.765
- Okay, so just between us,
I will admit it was my fault.

00:02:00.765 --> 00:02:01.650
(laughter)

00:02:01.650 --> 00:02:03.520
So we were high school sweethearts,

00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:08.030
and our freshman year in
college I was so excited.

00:02:08.030 --> 00:02:10.780
I'm an only child from
a pretty strict family,

00:02:10.780 --> 00:02:12.230
and I was like, oh my gosh.

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:14.280
We're gonna get out,
we're gonna have some fun,

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:16.540
we're gonna go party, we're
gonna let our hair down.

00:02:16.540 --> 00:02:17.986
And Troy was like yeah, no.

00:02:17.986 --> 00:02:21.480
I wanna be a police officer, I've got you,

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:23.400
you're like my life, I'm good.

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:24.770
And I was like, oh.

00:02:24.770 --> 00:02:25.830
I'm like, I don't think I could handle

00:02:25.830 --> 00:02:27.700
being married to a cop.

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:28.804
Which was great, because 18.

00:02:28.804 --> 00:02:30.260
- All the things you wanted didn't happen.

00:02:30.260 --> 00:02:32.330
- It didn't happen at
all, it was so silly.

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:34.960
18-year-old, I didn't
know what I wanted, so

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:36.940
it was a blessing in disguise, because

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:40.880
I got to go do I wanted and needed to do,

00:02:40.880 --> 00:02:43.020
and Troy got to follow his path

00:02:43.020 --> 00:02:45.610
in becoming a police
officer and everything.

00:02:45.610 --> 00:02:48.770
And he's truly my best friend.

00:02:48.770 --> 00:02:50.250
- Goals.

00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:52.030
So has Troy always been sentimental?

00:02:52.030 --> 00:02:53.910
Is he more the sentimental one than you?

00:02:53.910 --> 00:02:56.692
- He, well, yes.

00:02:56.692 --> 00:02:58.300
(audience laughing)

00:02:58.300 --> 00:02:59.457
- That was awesome.
- I can instruct

00:02:59.457 --> 00:03:00.910
how to be a sentimental, but he's

00:03:00.910 --> 00:03:02.300
really the one that does it.

00:03:02.300 --> 00:03:05.220
So even in high school,
he would write me poems.

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:06.820
- Do y'all ever, did y'all get poems,

00:03:06.820 --> 00:03:08.930
or did you write any poems?

00:03:08.930 --> 00:03:09.860
Ian?

00:03:09.860 --> 00:03:12.150
- I write some, my wife writes me notes

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:13.740
all the time and leaves them.

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:16.380
So I have to travel so much
too, but she writes notes,

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:18.960
and little pictures of her and the baby,

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:19.793
and it's really special.

00:03:19.793 --> 00:03:22.320
And I find them, like, in a boot.

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:24.810
I mean, she really has
gotten good at hiding them.

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:27.100
- My husband will do that,
he's really good at that.

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:28.920
- [Ian] It's so sweet.

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:30.570
- My husband writes songs for me.

00:03:31.467 --> 00:03:34.364
- You know what, pretty cool.
- I find that very romantic.

00:03:34.364 --> 00:03:35.197
I know.
- [Ian] I can't do that.

00:03:35.197 --> 00:03:37.130
- Yeah I don't write songs or do poems,

00:03:37.130 --> 00:03:38.361
so that's why I'm here.

00:03:38.361 --> 00:03:40.660
(audience laughing)
- Right, right!

00:03:40.660 --> 00:03:42.880
- So you wanted to go big and tell Troy

00:03:42.880 --> 00:03:44.560
how much you love him, why?

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:48.220
- I have not been that fabulous, I guess,

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:52.170
at expressing to him how
much he has meant to me

00:03:52.170 --> 00:03:56.070
through the last three
years that have just been

00:03:56.070 --> 00:03:57.530
roller coasters, up and down.

00:03:57.530 --> 00:04:00.920
And he's just my knight in shining armor,

00:04:00.920 --> 00:04:02.610
and I just--
- [Kelly] Partner in crime.

00:04:02.610 --> 00:04:05.370
- Yeah, and I felt like
reaching out to you guys

00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:07.950
to help me just go above and beyond,

00:04:07.950 --> 00:04:12.950
and do something to make
him laugh and have fun,

00:04:13.330 --> 00:04:16.660
and really feel how much he means,

00:04:16.660 --> 00:04:18.550
not only to me, but to everyone

00:04:18.550 --> 00:04:20.310
that he's come in touch with.

00:04:20.310 --> 00:04:21.653
He's always been such a wonderful person.

00:04:21.653 --> 00:04:24.749
(audience cheering)
- Yeah, he's a hero as well.

00:04:24.749 --> 00:04:26.640
Well, Shannon wanted to go big,

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:29.490
and I was happy to help, 'cause I'm Texan.

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:31.200
So I got together with my band,

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:32.930
and my friend Scott from Pentatonix,

00:04:32.930 --> 00:04:35.223
and we all had a musical
brainstorm session.

00:04:36.350 --> 00:04:37.469
Hello!

00:04:37.469 --> 00:04:40.440
(excited screaming)
This is Scott from Pentatonix.

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:41.830
We wanted to come help.

00:04:41.830 --> 00:04:43.960
- Aren't you so sweet!

00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:47.610
Oh my gosh, Kelly Clarkson
and Scott from Pentatonix

00:04:47.610 --> 00:04:48.840
just walked in this room.

00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:50.950
I can't express how excited I am

00:04:50.950 --> 00:04:53.740
writing a song for Troy with Kelly's band.

00:04:53.740 --> 00:04:55.850
- We know he's like, such
a here it is good dude,

00:04:55.850 --> 00:04:57.550
but we wanted to just
get some info from you

00:04:57.550 --> 00:05:00.240
from like, like how we
could kinda pull things

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:02.530
like from real life that he'd
laugh at and think are funny.

00:05:02.530 --> 00:05:05.070
- To have the opportunity
to share little parts

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:07.410
of Troy and I's life together,

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:09.790
it's just gonna be so much fun.

00:05:09.790 --> 00:05:11.540
- So does your husband have any nicknames

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:12.710
that we could possibly use?

00:05:12.710 --> 00:05:16.049
- My favorite nickname for
him is Cabana Boy Troy.

00:05:16.049 --> 00:05:18.640
- It's also my new favorite name.

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:20.150
- I've written several songs with Kelly,

00:05:20.150 --> 00:05:22.300
and most of the time
it's with radio in mind,

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:24.070
or fans in mind, so this is the first time

00:05:24.070 --> 00:05:26.204
I've written a song with
just one person in mind.

00:05:26.204 --> 00:05:29.380
- [Together] Cabana Boy
Troy, he ain't afraid to cry.

00:05:29.380 --> 00:05:32.115
Cabana Boy Troy.
- I love this song!

00:05:32.115 --> 00:05:32.948
(group cheering)

00:05:32.948 --> 00:05:36.440
- Watching them build this
song about Troy and I's life

00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:37.800
is more than incredible.

00:05:37.800 --> 00:05:39.720
- So when was your first kiss?

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:40.920
- Speaking of that, when did you have

00:05:40.920 --> 00:05:42.050
more than your first kiss?

00:05:42.050 --> 00:05:42.883
- Get it, get in there.
- Speaking of a good time!

00:05:42.883 --> 00:05:44.720
- Get in there, get in there.
(laughing)

00:05:44.720 --> 00:05:49.680
- Lemme just say that, the
movie The Little Mermaid

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:53.061
definitely stirs up some really good.

00:05:53.061 --> 00:05:54.351
- [Kelly] The Little Mermaid?

00:05:54.351 --> 00:05:56.333
- Yes.
- Not The Little Mermaid!

00:05:56.333 --> 00:05:58.470
- Clearly I'm not holding anything back.

00:05:58.470 --> 00:06:00.880
- Were you watching it when you?

00:06:00.880 --> 00:06:03.580
- Yeah, we were.
- Do you get a certain feeling

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:05.432
when you hear, like.
(steel drum music)

00:06:05.432 --> 00:06:06.840
(group laughing)

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:08.465
- Gets the hips moving.

00:06:08.465 --> 00:06:09.882
- That's going in the song!

00:06:09.882 --> 00:06:10.715
- My new favorite phrase right there.

00:06:10.715 --> 00:06:12.960
- Cabana Boy Troy, that, it all works.

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:16.110
- I'm having so much fun
with everyone in this room.

00:06:16.110 --> 00:06:16.943
- Oh my God, it'd actually be cool

00:06:16.943 --> 00:06:18.431
if it slowed down almost right there.

00:06:18.431 --> 00:06:19.880
- Part of your world!
- Or just me and you,

00:06:19.880 --> 00:06:21.730
and some kind of like, yeah, duet.

00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:24.020
- I can't wait to ambush Troy.

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:27.920
Because he is gonna connect
to every part of the song.

00:06:27.920 --> 00:06:29.561
He's not gonna know what happened.

00:06:29.561 --> 00:06:31.070
(audience applauding)

00:06:31.070 --> 00:06:34.530
- Oh my gosh, okay, so Shannon.

00:06:34.530 --> 00:06:37.650
Cabana Boy Troy, first of
all, thank you for that.

00:06:37.650 --> 00:06:40.020
That is awesome, it's a great hook.

00:06:40.020 --> 00:06:43.540
So how did he get the
nickname Cabana Boy Troy?

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:48.160
- So when we were younger,
I finally convinced him

00:06:48.160 --> 00:06:50.370
to start partying with
me, thank goodness, right?

00:06:50.370 --> 00:06:52.570
And he is a party and a half.

00:06:52.570 --> 00:06:55.690
So any time that we would
have people over to our house

00:06:55.690 --> 00:06:57.580
and hosting, he would make sure everybody

00:06:57.580 --> 00:07:00.000
was having a great time,
had a drink, had food.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:03.840
So it just came about, one
time he was bringing a drink,

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:05.830
and we're like oh, thanks cabana boy!

00:07:05.830 --> 00:07:08.140
And we're like, Cabana Boy Troy!

00:07:08.140 --> 00:07:11.220
That's what he is, and it's
been with him ever since.

00:07:11.220 --> 00:07:12.749
- I love it.

00:07:12.749 --> 00:07:14.253
(audience applauding)

00:07:14.253 --> 00:07:16.300
Well next, with the song all written,

00:07:16.300 --> 00:07:18.160
there was just one thing left to do.

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:19.510
Ambush Troy.

00:07:19.510 --> 00:07:21.710
So Shannon invited Troy to lunch

00:07:21.710 --> 00:07:23.410
at the place they go all the time,

00:07:23.410 --> 00:07:26.210
and he had no reason to
suspect anything was going on

00:07:26.210 --> 00:07:28.566
other than a nice meal, so just look.

00:07:28.566 --> 00:07:31.649
(rapid drum beating)

00:07:36.610 --> 00:07:37.762
- Well there's them.

00:07:37.762 --> 00:07:41.520
- [Kelly] That's them.
- [Woman] There at the bar.

00:07:41.520 --> 00:07:42.790
- Okay, got it.

00:07:42.790 --> 00:07:44.640
- We were sitting there,
and of course he's got

00:07:44.640 --> 00:07:47.370
Yoda in his lap, so Yoda's snoring.

00:07:47.370 --> 00:07:49.610
- We are about to ambush love song Troy.

00:07:49.610 --> 00:07:51.520
We're gonna ambush love
song the crap out of him.

00:07:51.520 --> 00:07:52.880
It's gonna be awesome.

00:07:52.880 --> 00:07:54.390
I'll go, are you Troy?

00:07:54.390 --> 00:07:56.010
All right buddy, this one's for you.

00:07:56.010 --> 00:07:58.410
Here we go, we're comin' in hot, Troy.

00:07:58.410 --> 00:07:59.243
- Go camera one!

00:07:59.243 --> 00:08:00.963
Go steady cam!

00:08:02.680 --> 00:08:05.303
- April and June are the trial holdings.

00:08:06.242 --> 00:08:08.889
I think April and June
are the trial dates.

00:08:08.889 --> 00:08:12.110
